MASTER ANTIGRAVITY PROMPT — HVAC DIGITAL TWIN & OPERATIONAL CONTROL PLATFORM
0. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

You are building a production-grade HVAC Digital Twin + Supervisory Monitoring + Control Platform.

This is NOT a generic HVAC dashboard.

This is NOT a static visualization.

This is NOT a collection of hard-coded mock screens.

This is NOT a frontend-only project.

The final system must represent a real physical HVAC installation as a dynamic, configuration-driven software digital twin, where physical equipment, components, sensors, actuators, relationships, telemetry, alarms, commands, communication health and historical data are represented as software entities.

The platform must be capable of initially operating entirely against a development/simulation environment, and later switching to the client's real MQTT/PLC infrastructure with minimal architectural changes.

The fundamental principle is:

The software must be driven by equipment metadata, topology, point definitions, configuration and live telemetry — never by hard-coded equipment assumptions.

The current Stitch designs are the visual and interaction reference.

They are NOT the source of truth for actual equipment topology or telemetry.

The actual HVAC configuration must come from the application's data/configuration model.

