Real-time delivery

WebSocket.

Visualization

Frontend digital twin.

Never let the frontend become the source of truth for physical equipment state.

74. IMPORTANT DISTINCTION

Do not confuse:

Equipment State

with:

Communication State

Example:

Fan:
RUNNING

Communication:
OFFLINE

This should not automatically be interpreted as:

Fan is stopped

Instead:

Last known state: RUNNING
Communication: OFFLINE
Data quality: STALE

This distinction is critical for industrial monitoring.

75. COMMAND CONFIRMATION

When the operator requests:

START FAN

UI should show:

Command requested
      ↓
Command sent
      ↓
Waiting for equipment confirmation
      ↓
Equipment RUNNING

If confirmation doesn't arrive:

Command timeout

Do not simply change the UI to RUNNING because the user clicked START.

76. ALARM ACKNOWLEDGEMENT

Acknowledging an alarm does NOT mean clearing it.

Maintain:

ACTIVE + ACKNOWLEDGED

until the actual condition clears.

The UI must communicate this correctly.

77. NO INVENTED HVAC LOGIC

